# External live-PID rendezvous first slice — NOT ADMISSION

Engineer source only. The exact upstream design is SHA-256 `5dcca56caf8ad0e9f61da30c0085173e33316e84bd59fb72940186da8a80e5d8`. The Node program is builtin-only and has no self-`/proc` read, package root, SDK or SQL. The Python caller and entry refuse unconditionally. Keeper05 creation07 is a separate refusing source contract; no leaf, runner, birth, permit or admission was created.

The one connected stream would emit READY (closed9), consume START (closed6), emit RESULT (closed9), consume EXIT (closed6), require EOF, then exit0. Exact UTF-8 compact JSON plus one LF is the frame encoding. The `runtimeFenceSha256` input is SHA-256 over compact UTF-8 JSON without LF and exactly these READY fields in order: `node`, `logicalArgv`, `processEnv`, `embeddedLoaders`, `scriptSha256`. The caller compares RESULT to retained READY bytes, sent START bytes, and the PRE_START attestation. PRE_START and POST_RESULT attestations use the same closed18-key ordered record from `attestation()`; SHA covers `output_frame(record)` including LF. Raw helper outputs must be retained separately.

The pure helper schema requires six ordered roles: statBefore, cmdline, environ, exeLink, exeHash, statAfter. Each requires an independently source-bound exact argv/executable identity, CID, distinct numeric PID, two matching live stat PID/PPID/startTicks records, exact NUL argv/env, and a sorted unique process inventory containing only inert PID1, candidate PID and that helper PID. This is a source contract, not actual helper provenance. Helper binaries, real Bash/exec continuity, inventory reads, and target proc visibility remain unobserved. Arbitrary helper authority supplied to a pure test does not authorize runtime use.

A future caller must implement one 900-second monotonic budget, <=30-second helpers, <=250ms polls, bounded incremental stream reads, durable raw receipts before START/EXIT, source and birth rehashes, signal/partial-write/cleanup quarantine, qualified same-CID stop, and independent CLOSED readback. This first slice has no live orchestration and cannot establish those properties. Any first actual attempt requires fresh keeper05 creation and independent birth, observed exact toolchain bytes, source and artifact reviews, issued one-use permit/admission, and a separate exact outer launch. No prior keeper or failed method is reusable.
